<% content_for :title, "Demo 4: MCP Scheduler + MCP Persistence" %>

<div class="container py-5">

  <%# Back to Home %>
  <div class="row mb-3">
    <div class="col">
      <%= link_to root_path, class: "btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" do %>
        <i class="bi bi-arrow-left me-1"></i> Back to Demo Selection
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Hero Section %>
  <div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto text-center">
      <span class="badge mb-3 fs-6 text-white" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6f42c1 0%, #9c6ade 100%);">Demo 4</span>
      <h1 class="display-5 fw-bold mb-3">
        <i class="bi bi-clock-history me-2" style="color: #6f42c1;"></i>
        MCP Scheduler + MCP Persistence
      </h1>
      <p class="lead text-muted">
        Connect an AIsuru agent to the platform's built-in <strong>Scheduler</strong> and
        <strong>Persistence</strong> MCP servers &mdash; no self-hosted backend required for this demo.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm" style="border-left: 4px solid #6f42c1 !important;">
        <div class="card-body">
          <h5 class="fw-bold mb-3">
            <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-2" style="color: #6f42c1;"></i>
            About this demo
          </h5>
          <p class="text-muted mb-2">
            <strong>MCP Scheduler</strong> lets the agent schedule a tool call to run at a later time
            (e.g. a reminder, a follow-up action, a recurring check).
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted mb-0">
            <strong>MCP Persistence</strong> lets the agent store and retrieve structured data across
            turns and sessions, instead of relying only on conversation history.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# The one thing that makes this demo different from Demo 1-3: there is no
      embedded chat here, and the reason is a platform constraint rather than
      an omission. Say it early and say it plainly, same as Demo 7. %>
  <div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="alert alert-warning border-warning d-flex mb-0">
        <i class="bi bi-shield-lock-fill me-3 fs-4 text-warning"></i>
        <div>
          <strong>This demo runs inside AIsuru, not in an embedded chat.</strong>
          <p class="text-muted mb-2 small">
            A scheduled task has to reach a conversation that is still there when it fires &mdash;
            seconds, minutes, or hours later &mdash; and its result has to persist in the agent's own
            store across that gap. That requires the stable, signed-in identity of the agent's own
            chat on AIsuru. An embedded web component on a public page is a different, disposable
            session: it will not reliably be there when the task runs, so Scheduler and Persistence
            are not exercised through it in this demo.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted mb-0 small">
            Everything else on this page stays exactly the same: the setup, the servers to add, the
            prompt to try.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Setup Instructions %>
  <div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="card" style="border-color: #6f42c1;">
        <div class="card-header text-white" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6f42c1 0%, #9c6ade 100%);">
          <h5 class="mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-tools me-2"></i>
            Setup Instructions: Scheduler + Persistence
          </h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
          <p class="text-muted mb-4">
            Both MCP servers used in this demo are built into AIsuru &mdash; there is nothing to run
            or expose locally, you just need to enable them on your agent.
          </p>

          <%# Step 1 %>
          <div class="d-flex mb-4">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
              <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6f42c1 0%, #9c6ade 100%);">1</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex-grow-1">
              <h6 class="fw-bold">Create an Agent on AIsuru</h6>
              <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                Create a new agent on <a href="https://www.aisuru.com" target="_blank">AIsuru</a>
                (or reuse an existing one, including the one from a previous demo).
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <%# Step 2 %>
          <div class="d-flex mb-4">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
              <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6f42c1 0%, #9c6ade 100%);">2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex-grow-1">
              <h6 class="fw-bold">Add the Scheduler and Persistence MCP servers</h6>
              <p class="text-muted mb-2">
                Open your agent in AIsuru and go to the <strong>MCP</strong> section.
                From the catalog of built-in servers, add:
              </p>
              <ul class="text-muted mb-2">
                <li><strong>MCP Scheduler</strong></li>
                <li><strong>MCP Persistence</strong></li>
              </ul>
              <small class="text-muted">
                Both are ready-made platform servers &mdash; no connection string or credentials to fill
                in, just add them from the list and save.
              </small>
            </div>
          </div>

          <%# Step 3 %>
          <div class="d-flex mb-4">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
              <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6f42c1 0%, #9c6ade 100%);">3</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex-grow-1">
              <h6 class="fw-bold">Open the agent's chat on AIsuru</h6>
              <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                Stay signed in and open your agent's own chat on AIsuru. That is where the rest of
                this demo happens. There is no <code>memoriID</code> to paste and no agent to load
                on this page.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <%# Step 4 %>
          <div class="d-flex mb-3">
            <div class="flex-shrink-0 me-3">
              <span class="badge rounded-circle fs-5 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center text-white" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6f42c1 0%, #9c6ade 100%);">4</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex-grow-1">
              <h6 class="fw-bold">Try it: schedule a recurring task and watch it persist</h6>
              <p class="text-muted mb-2">
                In the agent's chat, ask it to run a task on a recurring schedule with a minimum
                interval of <strong>1 minute</strong> using MCP Scheduler, and to save the result of
                each run using MCP Persistence:
              </p>
              <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded mb-2"><code>Every minute, run a task and save its result using the persistence tool.</code></pre>
              <p class="text-muted mb-2">
                You can check what's actually being saved in two ways:
              </p>
              <ul class="text-muted mb-2">
                <li>
                  Ask the agent to read back what it last saved (e.g.
                  <em>"what's the last value you saved?"</em>).
                </li>
                <li>
                  Or see it directly, without going through the agent: go back to the
                  <strong>MCP</strong> section, find the <strong>MCP Persistence</strong> server
                  you added in Step 2, and click its <strong>Dashboard</strong> button &mdash; it
                  opens a view of the stored data as the MCP server sees it.
                </li>
              </ul>
              <p class="text-muted mb-0">
                Reload that dashboard every minute or so: you should see the saved value change on
                its own &mdash; confirming the scheduled task is really running in the background and
                updating storage every minute, not just when you're chatting with the agent.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Where the demo actually happens. %>
  <div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-10 mx-auto">
      <div class="d-grid">
        <a href="https://www.aisuru.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
           class="btn btn-lg text-white" style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6f42c1 0%, #9c6ade 100%);">
          <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-up-right me-2"></i>
          Open your agent on AIsuru
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="text-center text-muted small mt-2 mb-0">
        Signed in as the agent's owner. Keep this page open beside it for the setup steps above.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
